# Activity reporting (MYHR)

After meaningful work, end of session, or when user asks for a report — output copy-paste blocks in tracker format below.

Same format as REPORTING / PTW trackers. Project name is always `MYHR` (one project for `myhr-frontend`, `myhr-backend`, legacy `myhr_api`, legacy `myhrs`).

## Add item first

Items **must exist** before `/report`. If missing, output `/add item` blocks first — never `/report` alone.
Check **Tracker memory (state)** at the bottom: if `category + name` is listed there, it already exists → `/report` only.

## Categories (exact spelling)

| Category    | Scope                                                              |
| ----------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------ |
| `Front End` | React pages, components, hooks, context, services, layout, routing |
| `Back End`  | Express routes, controllers, middleware, services, API             |
| `Database`  | `scripts/hr/*.sql`, SP, views, migrations, seeds, Azure sync       |
| `Other`     | Docs (`AGENTS.md`, `README`), deploy, `.env.example`, non-code     |

## Item = module scope, not task detail

Keep Gantt lean: **item name = broad module** (1 Gantt row). Put daily specifics in the **notes** field (after last `|`).

| Bad (too specific)             | Good (scope)      | Notes in `/report`                                        |
| ------------------------------ | ----------------- | --------------------------------------------------------- |
| Fix Sakit Evidence Upload      | Sakit             | multipart bukti upload + evidence_paths on SELECT/GET     |
| API Pola Kerja Generate Roster | Pola Kerja        | GENERATE_PREVIEW / GENERATE in POLA_KERJA_SP + endpoints  |
| Level Permissions Matrix Page  | Level Permissions | matrix editor, superadmin-only PUT                        |

Rules:

- **1 scope = 1 Gantt row** — merge sub-tasks under same parent item.
- Item name: **1–3 words** (`Login`, `Users`, `Menus`, `Sakit`, `Pola Kerja`, `Dashboard`).
- No `Fix`, `API`, `Halaman`, `Redeploy`, `SP`, `Script` in item name — put in notes.
- Continuation work → update existing scope item, do not create new item.
- Same scope in FE + BE + DB → one item per category with the **same name** (e.g. `Sakit` ×3).

## `/add item` format

**One block, one or many items.** Write `project` once at the top; repeat the field group per item (each item starts with `category`).

```
/add item
project : MYHR

category : Front End
name : Sakit
start date : 2026-10-10
end date : 2026-10-17
weight : 8
priority : HIGH
pic : 0216691
type : NEW

category : Back End
name : Sakit
start date : 2026-10-10
end date : 2026-10-17
weight : 8
priority : HIGH
pic : 0216691
type : NEW

category : Database
name : Sakit
start date : 2026-10-10
end date : 2026-10-17
weight : 6
priority : HIGH
pic : 0216691
type : NEW
```

- Blank line between items is optional.
- Per item: `category`, `name`, `start date`, `end date`, `weight`, `priority`, `pic`, `type` — each may differ.
- `name` must match exactly in `/add item` and `/report`.
- `type`: `NEW` | `MODIFIKASI`; `priority`: `LOW` | `MEDIUM` | `HIGH`.
- **`MODIFIKASI`** — item was already **100%** and work resumed; re-`/add item` with this type (not `UPDATE`).
- Default `pic : 0216691`. Dates `YYYY-MM-DD`; `end date` = realistic estimate, not today by default.
- Prefer **one multi-item block** when registering several scopes at once.

## `/report` format

```
/report
project : MYHR

category : Back End
user : 0216691
task :
Sakit | 60>85 | CANCEL action + evidence download endpoint
Dashboard | 90>100 | ATTENDANCE computed in hr; parity dbo vs hr OK

status : UPDATE
```

- Progress: `before>after` (0–100). Notes = today's specific work.
- **Item complete:** always `before>100 | notes` (after = `100`).
- One line per scope item; group by category (one `category` block per category, each with its own `user` / `task`).

## Tracker memory (agent)

1. Remember reported items and last progress per `category + name` → table **Tracker memory (state)** below.
2. After the user confirms a `/report` was sent, update that table (this is the only rule edit allowed without asking).
3. User says item is **complete** → `/report` with `before>100 | notes`.
4. Item already **100%** and changes again → `/add item` with `type: MODIFIKASI` first, then `/report`.
5. Copies of this rule exist in `myhr-frontend`, `myhr_api`, `myhrs`; the **state table lives only here** (`myhr-backend`).

## When to offer report

1. After meaningful feature/fix (not every small commit).
2. User asks for a report (`report`, `tracker`, `progress`).
3. End of long session.

